manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD does not take over s2's file-commit work or s3's single entity remove function: export_names upkeep is added inside the existing detachDeleteEntitiesInTxn, and incoming-edge return-to-pending is limited to cross-repository edges at repository reindex","evidence":"Adjacent scope lists s2 as owning 'incoming relationships of a removed entity returned to pending' within the file commit, and s3 as owning one put/remove function. §3.3 places the cleanup in detachDeleteEntitiesInTxn (entities.ts:1099), which exists today, and says s3 consumes it unchanged. §2.13 adds returnIncomingToPending only on deleteEntitiesForRepo (entities.ts:560) for other repositories' edges. The file-event path (index.ts:784-787) and reindexFile (:485) are left as they are. [files: src/db/entities.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A daemon crash mid full index is detectable at start-up and re-queued by extending the existing start-up rule (index.ts:286-300); a failing cross-file pass propagates to status 'error' as today","evidence":"index.ts:287-300 enqueues `{ kind: 'full' }` for status pending, error, or indexing without lastIndexed, so it can be extended with an IndexState check. fullIndex :706-707 awaits runCrossFileResolver inside the try, and the catch at :760-764 writes status 'error' with lastRunOf('failed'). The endpoint passes have their own try/catch at :715-734, where endpointPassFailed would be set. indexFile returns false on a read failure (:1028-1029) and fullIndex counts it only as skipped (:655-656), as the LLD states. [files: src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","